From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:38:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 258/342] meson_gpio: Hardkernel's 16x2 LCD + IO Shield as
 /dev/misc/shield

With "lcd_io_shield true" in meson_gpio's driver settings (the shield
can't be detected), three devices on the header's pins, as the shield's
schematic has them (headers/private/drivers/lcd_shield.h):

- lcd: the HD44780 display in 4-bit mode, written only (its R/W is
  tied low), with the datasheet's times instead of the busy flag. Text
  in UTF-8, mapped to the A00 character set; '\n' goes to the next line
  and clears it, scrolling from the second, once something follows it;
  '\r', '\f', '\b', '\t'; eight user characters. Reading it gives the
  two lines. ioctls for the cursor, the position, clearing, the display
  and the codes shown.
- leds: D1 to D7, written and read as "1010101".
- buttons: SW1 and SW2 with the pins' pull-ups, sampled every 10 ms
  while open and debounced over two samples; reading gives "SW1
  pressed" lines, every open file all events; an ioctl waits for one.

The pins are claimed from meson_header as "LCD shield" when a device is
first opened and kept. The shield uses meson_gpio through new in-kernel
calls (ClaimPins, SetOutputs, WriteLevels, ReadLevels, SetPulls); the
class moved to MesonGpio.h for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
